Mascot artwork — brand asset, not open source
=============================================

The images under assets/mascots/ are artwork owned by DZ23. They are brand assets of the B-3PO BOT PLATFORM and are
NOT licensed for reuse, redistribution or modification. This notice covers the image files only.

Everything else in this repository — including the code that names, validates, derives and displays these images — is
licensed under the Apache License 2.0, as stated in the repository's LICENSE file. The Apache licence does not extend to
the artwork.

The artwork carries no name and no role: a mascot is an identity a person picks for a bot, never a job title. Roles and
teams are configuration in the host, not something baked into a picture.

This is a project decision about ownership, not a legal clearance. Before any public launch, distribution or marketing
spend, the trademark question is checked separately (master goal, section 14).
